# Common Rules

## Core Working Rules

1. This project runs with Poetry. Always use `poetry run ...` for project commands.
2. Follow SOLID principles and clean code conventions.
3. The documentation entry point is `README.md`, which links to detailed docs in `docs/`.
4. After code changes, run `poetry run pre-commit run --all-files` to verify quality gates.

## Rule Priority (Conflict Resolution)

When instructions conflict, apply this priority order:

1. Feature specs in `docs/specs/001-housemaid-booking-api/spec.md` and related module specs
2. Task-specific project rules (for example, `add-new-api.mdc`)
3. Architecture rules (`architecture.mdc`)
4. Common rules (`common.mdc`)
5. Generic skills/templates in `.agents/skills`
